WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.410
Let me show you Runway, built for the

2
00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:06.669
Consumer Finance track. When you freelance for stablecoins,

3
00:00:06.669 --> 00:00:09.929
a late invoice can leave rent uncovered, even

4
00:00:09.929 --> 00:00:12.374
when your expected income looks healthy.

5
00:00:12.704 --> 00:00:16.281
I am connecting the supplied Sui wallet and

6
00:00:16.281 --> 00:00:19.857
signing Runway’s login message. This opens a private

7
00:00:19.857 --> 00:00:22.987
workspace. The signature does not transfer funds.

8
00:00:23.317 --> 00:00:26.176
Here I refresh the wallet through Tatum on

9
00:00:26.176 --> 00:00:29.034
Sui Mainnet. This is the actual balance, separate

10
00:00:29.034 --> 00:00:31.893
from the example we are about to run.

11
00:00:32.223 --> 00:00:36.008
Now let’s open the labelled example. Eight hundred

12
00:00:36.008 --> 00:00:39.793
USDC is confirmed. Twelve hundred is still expected.

13
00:00:39.793 --> 00:00:43.578
We have a Saturday purchase, Monday rent, and

14
00:00:43.578 --> 00:00:45.471
a hundred USDC reserve.

15
00:00:45.801 --> 00:00:49.172
On the client’s promised Friday, the projection covers

16
00:00:49.172 --> 00:00:52.542
rent. But an unpaid invoice is still a

17
00:00:52.542 --> 00:00:55.913
promise. It never increases the money available now.

18
00:00:56.243 --> 00:00:59.799
Switch to past payments. Four invoices arrived three,

19
00:00:59.799 --> 00:01:03.354
four, four, and five days late. That moves

20
00:01:03.354 --> 00:01:06.910
Friday to Tuesday, after rent. The smallest permitted

21
00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:10.465
fix is reducing the flexible purchase by a

22
00:01:10.465 --> 00:01:12.243
hundred and fifty USDC.

23
00:01:12.573 --> 00:01:15.694
Here is the evidence behind that decision: which

24
00:01:15.694 --> 00:01:18.815
past payments were used, the observed range, and

25
00:01:18.815 --> 00:01:21.935
the median delay. You can inspect the reason

26
00:01:21.935 --> 00:01:23.496
before accepting the plan.

27
00:01:23.825 --> 00:01:26.890
The no-payment stress test checks the downside too.

28
00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:29.956
I review the change: the purchase drops from

29
00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:33.021
two hundred and fifty to one hundred. Rent

30
00:01:33.021 --> 00:01:33.788
stays fixed.

31
00:01:34.118 --> 00:01:37.381
I save the plan and reload. The change

32
00:01:37.381 --> 00:01:40.644
survives. We have preserved the reserve without treating

33
00:01:40.644 --> 00:01:43.907
expected income as cash, and without moving any

34
00:01:43.907 --> 00:01:44.315
funds.

35
00:01:44.645 --> 00:01:48.596
Now I click Recall from Walrus. This makes

36
00:01:48.596 --> 00:01:52.547
a real Mainnet request for the published synthetic

37
00:01:52.547 --> 00:01:56.499
records. Their identifiers and content hashes must match.

38
00:01:56.499 --> 00:02:00.450
The recalled history reproduces the same hundred-and-fifty USDC

39
00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:00.944
decision.

40
00:02:01.274 --> 00:02:04.950
Memory must also remember corrections. The recalled reserve

41
00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:08.627
update changes the reduction to one hundred USDC.

42
00:02:08.627 --> 00:02:12.303
A separate client correction removes the wrong payment

43
00:02:12.303 --> 00:02:15.979
from that history, so an old fact cannot

44
00:02:15.979 --> 00:02:18.277
quietly drive the next forecast.

45
00:02:18.607 --> 00:02:22.217
This is the Consumer Finance idea: separate cash

46
00:02:22.217 --> 00:02:25.828
from promises, protect bills before a late payment,

47
00:02:25.828 --> 00:02:29.438
and carry payment lessons between sessions. The replay

48
00:02:29.438 --> 00:02:33.048
publishes its misses too. Runway gives freelancers a

49
00:02:33.048 --> 00:02:36.207
decision they can inspect, review, and keep.
